=== Layer 1 - Physical Layer
*Cables, connectors, topologies, signals*

The Physical Layer is the foundation of the OSI model. It is responsible for the transmission of raw bits over a physical medium, whether that is copper wire, fiber optic cable, or radio waves. It does not understand what the data means; it simply moves ones and zeros from one point to another. This is distinct from the unoficial layer 0. Whereas layer 0 describes the background propogation of electricity and waves in the material itself, layer 1 translates this into signal that is interpreted as information. To do this job, Layer 1 is divided into three sublayers, each handling a distinct part of the process.

- PMD, PMA, PCS sublayers
- Line encoding schemes (NRZ, PAM-4, 8b/10b, 64b/66b) and why they matter
- Cable selection (copper vs. fiber) and EM eavesdropping surface

==== The Three Sublayers and How They Interact

